  "result": "Perfect! All 181 tests pass. I've successfully added a customer statement generator.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Created src/statements.js** with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)`:\n   - Generates a customer statement showing outstanding invoices\n   - Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n   - Normalizes customer ID for matching\n   - Filters invoices by:\n     - Matching customer ID\n     - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n     - Issue date on or before cutoff date (asOf)\n   - Each invoice includes: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n   - Calculates due amount using `balanceDue()`\n   - Sorts by issueDate ascending\n   - Sums all due amounts to get totalDue\n   - Returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for unknown customers\n   - Returns DATE_INVALID for invalid asOf date\n\n2. **Added 15 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Invoice retrieval and filtering\n   - Customer ID normalization\n   - Date cutoff filtering (before, on, after)\n   - Status filtering (excludes draft, paid, includes issued/partially_paid)\n   - Multi-invoice sorting and totaling\n   - Zero results handling\n   - All required fields in statement\n\nThe statement correctly calculates outstanding balances and provides a clear view of customer payment obligations as of any given date.",
